Supreme People's Court Issuance

Notice of the  
Provisional Regulations on Case Filing for Criminal Compensation and Non-Criminal Judicial Compensation Cases (for Trial Implementation)  
Provisional Regulations on Causes of Action for Criminal Compensation and Non-Criminal Judicial Compensation Cases (for Trial Implementation)  
and the  
Style of Documents for State Compensation Cases (for Trial Implementation)

Fa Fa [2000] No. 2

All local people's courts at various levels throughout the country, all military courts at various levels, all railway transport intermediate courts and basic level courts, all maritime courts, and all courts at various levels in the Xinjiang Production and Construction Corps:

The "Provisional Regulations on Case Filing for Criminal Compensation and Non-Criminal Judicial Compensation Cases (for Trial Implementation)," the "Provisional Regulations on Causes of Action for Criminal Compensation and Non-Criminal Judicial Compensation Cases (for Trial Implementation)," and the "Style of Documents for State Compensation Cases (for Trial Implementation)" were discussed and adopted at the ninth meeting of the Compensation Committee of this Court. They are hereby issued to you for trial implementation. Please earnestly comply and implement them. If you have any opinions or problems during implementation, please promptly report them to the Compensation Committee of this Court.

January 11, 2000

Attached:

Provisional Regulations on Case Filing for Criminal Compensation and Non-Criminal Judicial Compensation Cases (for Trial Implementation)

Article 1: The case filing work for compensation cases shall be conducted in a manner conducive to the correct and timely adjudication of cases by the people's court or the compensation committee of the people's court.

Article 2: The people's court or the compensation committee of the people's court shall conduct a review of the compensation application submitted by the compensation claimant in accordance with the law. If the conditions for case acceptance are met, the case shall be filed.

Article 3: When a compensation claimant submits a compensation application to the people's court or the compensation committee of the people's court, the judicial infringement act of the compensatory obligor shall first have been confirmed in accordance with the law.

Article 4: The case filing work for a compensation case in which the people's court at the same level is the compensatory obligor shall be handled by the case filing division of that court.

Article 5: The scope of case filing for a compensation case in which the people's court at the same level is the compensatory obligor is as follows:

(1) Where an arrest is wrongly decided against a person who has no criminal facts;
(2) Where, upon retrial in accordance with the trial supervision procedure, the person is acquitted, but the original sentence has already been executed;
(3) Where extortion of confessions by torture, or violent acts such as assault, or instigating others to commit violent acts such as assault, or illegal use of weapons or police instruments cause bodily injury or death to a citizen;
(4) Where the people's court illegally takes measures such as sealing up, distraining, freezing, or recovery of property, causing damage;
(5) Where, upon retrial in accordance with the trial supervision procedure, the person is acquitted, but the original fine or confiscation of property has already been executed;
(6) Where a first-instance judgment finds guilt, but the second-instance judgment acquits;
(7) Where, during civil litigation or administrative litigation, the people's court illegally takes coercive measures or preservation measures to impede litigation, or makes errors in executing judgments, rulings, or other effective legal instruments, causing damage.

Article 6: After receiving a party's compensation application, the people's court shall conduct a review in accordance with the law. If the following conditions are met, the case shall be filed:

(1) The compensation claimant shall possess the legal capacity to be a party;
(2) The court is the compensatory obligor;
(3) There are specific compensation claims and factual grounds;
(4) There are legal instruments confirming the infringement or other evidentiary materials;
(5) The application is made within the statutory time limit for claims, except where force majeure or other obstacles prevent the exercise of the claim within the statutory period, or where the people's court has decided to extend the period.

Article 7: The case filing work for a compensation case that is to be decided by the compensation committee of the people's court in accordance with the law shall be handled by the office of the compensation committee.

Article 8: The scope of case filing for a compensation case accepted by the compensation committee of the people's court is as follows:

(1) Where, because the criminal suspect has no criminal facts or the facts are unclear and evidence insufficient, the investigative authority releases the criminal suspect from criminal detention, or the procuratorial authority does not approve arrest, or the investigative authority withdraws the case and decides to release the person;
(2) Where, because the criminal suspect has no criminal facts or the facts are unclear and evidence insufficient, the procuratorial authority makes a decision to cancel a detention decision, a decision not to approve arrest, a decision to cancel an arrest, a decision to withdraw the case, or a decision not to prosecute;
(3) Where, because the criminal suspect has no criminal facts or the facts are unclear and evidence insufficient, the people's court cancels an arrest decision;
(4) Where the people's court renders a first-instance judgment of acquittal that has become legally effective, a second-instance judgment of acquittal, or upon retrial in accordance with the trial supervision procedure, a judgment of acquittal that has become legally effective;
(5) Where an investigative, procuratorial, judicial, or prison administration authority or its functionaries commit acts specified in Article 15, items (4) and (5) of the State Compensation Law, and the responsible persons have been held criminally liable or subjected to other sanctions;
(6) Where acts specified in Article 16 of the State Compensation Law have been committed and have been corrected in accordance with the law;
(7) Where the people's court cancels an original erroneous judicial detention or fine decision;
(8) Where the people's court cancels an original erroneous summons by force;
(9) Where the people's court cancels an original erroneous property preservation ruling;
(10) Where the people's court erroneously executes judgments, rulings, or other effective legal instruments, and such errors have been corrected in accordance with the law;
(11) Where a higher people's court, upon reconsideration, cancels an original erroneous coercive measure, preservation measure, execution ruling, or decision of a lower people's court;
(12) Other circumstances where an investigative, procuratorial, judicial, or prison administration authority has corrected illegal infringements in accordance with the law.

Article 9: After receiving a compensation application, the compensation committee of the people's court shall conduct a review in accordance with the law. If the following conditions are met, the case shall be filed:

(1) The compensation claimant possesses the legal capacity to be a party;
(2) The compensatory obligor is an authority exercising powers of investigation, prosecution, adjudication, or prison administration;
(3) There are specific compensation claims and factual grounds;
(4) There are legal instruments confirming the infringement or other evidentiary materials;
(5) The application is made within the statutory time limit for claims, except where force majeure or other obstacles prevent the exercise of the claim within the statutory period, or where the compensation committee of the people's court has decided to extend the period;
(6) Where the compensatory obligor is an investigative, procuratorial, or prison administration authority, the compensation claimant, after a compensation decision is made or after the authority fails to make a compensation decision within the time limit, applies for reconsideration, and is still dissatisfied after reconsideration, or the reconsideration authority fails to make a reconsideration decision within the time limit; where the compensatory obligor is a people's court, the compensation claimant is dissatisfied with the compensation decision made by that court, or the court fails to make a compensation decision within the time limit;
(7) The requirements of the State Compensation Law and relevant judicial interpretations concerning the retroactive effect of the State Compensation Law are satisfied.

Article 10: The people's court or the compensation committee of the people's court shall, within seven days from the date of receiving the compensation application, decide whether to file the case or to refuse to accept the application.

Article 11: When reviewing for case filing, if it is found that relevant evidentiary materials are missing, the compensation claimant shall be notified to supplement them. The date of receipt of the compensation application shall be calculated from the date when the relevant evidentiary materials are fully supplemented.

Article 12: If a decision to file the case is made, a case number shall be assigned, a case filing registration form shall be filled out, and a notice of acceptance of the case shall be issued to the compensation claimant.

If the compensation committee of the people's court decides to file the case, it shall also issue a notice of acceptance of the case to the compensatory obligor and the reconsideration authority, and shall serve a copy of the compensation application.

Article 13: If the people's court decides to file the case, the case filing division shall transfer the case to the relevant department within two days, complete the handover procedures, and indicate the date of transfer. The date of registration of the decision to file the case after review shall be the date of case filing.

Article 14: If, after review, the conditions for case filing are not met, a notice of refusal to accept the case shall be prepared.

Article 15: The compensation committee of a higher people's court shall supervise and guide the case filing work of the people's court or the compensation committee of the lower people's court.

Article 16: If, after review, it is found that the case should not be accepted by the people's court or the compensation committee of the people's court, the compensation claimant shall be informed to apply for compensation to the relevant authority.

Provisional Regulations on Causes of Action for Criminal Compensation and Non-Criminal Judicial Compensation Cases (for Trial Implementation)

Article 1: These provisional regulations are formulated in accordance with the provisions of the State Compensation Law of the People's Republic of China (hereinafter referred to as the State Compensation Law) to standardize the causes of action for criminal compensation and non-criminal judicial compensation cases.

1. Compensation for Wrongful Criminal Detention [Article 15, Item (1) of the State Compensation Law]: Compensation cases for the wrongful detention of a person who has no criminal facts or for whom there is no evidence to suggest a major criminal suspect.

2. Compensation for Wrongful Arrest [Article 15, Item (2) of the State Compensation Law]: Compensation cases for the wrongful arrest of a person who has no criminal facts.

3. Joint Compensation for Wrongful Arrest and Wrongful Conviction [Article 15, Item (2) and Article 19, Paragraph 4 of the State Compensation Law]: Compensation cases where a person with no criminal facts is wrongfully arrested, and the court of first instance renders a guilty verdict while the court of second instance declares acquittal.

4. Compensation for Acquittal upon Retrial [Article 15, Item (3) of the State Compensation Law]: Compensation cases where, upon retrial in accordance with the trial supervision procedure, the person is acquitted, but the original sentence has already been executed.

5. Compensation for Injury or Death Caused by Extortion of Confessions by Torture [Article 15, Item (4) of the State Compensation Law]: Compensation cases where extortion of confessions by torture causes bodily injury or death to a citizen.

6. Compensation for Injury or Death Caused by Use of Violence or Instigating Others to Use Violence [Article 15, Item (4) of the State Compensation Law]: Compensation cases where violent acts such as assault, or instigating others to commit violent acts such as assault, cause bodily injury or death to a citizen.

7. Compensation for Injury or Death Caused by Illegal Use of Weapons or Police Instruments [Article 15, Item (5) of the State Compensation Law]: Compensation cases where illegal use of weapons or police instruments causes injury or death to a citizen.

8. Compensation for Illegal Sealing, Distraining, Freezing, or Recovery of Property in Criminal Cases [Article 16, Item (1) of the State Compensation Law]: Compensation cases where, during criminal proceedings, coercive measures such as sealing up, distraining, freezing, or recovery of property are illegally taken.

9. Compensation for Wrongful Fine or Confiscation of Property [Article 16, Item (2) of the State Compensation Law]: Compensation cases where, upon retrial in accordance with the trial supervision procedure, the person is acquitted, but the original fine or confiscation of property has already been executed.

10. Compensation for Illegal Judicial Summons by Force [Article 31 of the State Compensation Law]: Compensation for illegal summons by force by a people's court during civil or administrative proceedings.

11. Compensation for Illegal Judicial Fine [Article 31 of the State Compensation Law]: Compensation cases for illegal fines by a people's court during civil or administrative proceedings.

12. Compensation for Illegal Judicial Detention [Article 31 of the State Compensation Law]: Compensation cases for illegal judicial detention by a people's court during civil or administrative proceedings.

13. Compensation for Illegal Sealing, Distraining, or Freezing [Article 31 of the State Compensation Law]: Compensation cases where a people's court illegally takes preservation measures such as sealing up, distraining, or freezing (including other methods prescribed by law) during civil or administrative proceedings.

14. Compensation for Erroneous Execution [Article 31 of the State Compensation Law]: Compensation cases where a people's court makes errors in executing judgments, rulings, or other effective legal instruments during civil or administrative proceedings.

Style of Documents for State Compensation Cases (for Trial Implementation) (Omitted)
